        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "232515b2-170a-5cc1-85eb-3c4b48974e89",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: George Frideric Handel\n- Works: Sosarme, re di Media; Sosarmes, King of Media\n- Places: London; King's Theatre in the Haymarket; Halle; Hamburg; Italy\n- Topics: opera; baroque music; naturalisation\n\nFacts:\n- George Frideric Handel was born on 23 February 1685 (O.S.) and became a German-born, later British, baroque composer.\n- George Frideric Handel received important training in Halle and later worked as a composer in Hamburg and Italy before settling in London in 1712.\n- George Frideric Handel became a naturalised British subject in 1727.\n- In 1732, George Frideric Handel wrote the opera Sosarme, re di Media (\"Sosarmes, King of Media\", HWV 30) for the King's Theatre in the Haymarket in London.\n- Sosarme, re di Media ran for 12 performances at the King's Theatre in the Haymarket in London.\n- George Frideric Handel spent most of his career in London and became well known for his operas, oratorios, anthems, and organ concertos.\n- George Frideric Handel died on 14 April 1759.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
